{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "01W0", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:7c4b7f1483a6f0c8c2a87d2110be465962e13648bb17ef2e915ed0d25f17ba22", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThe following lemma says that the image of a proper scheme (in a separated\nscheme of finite type over the base) is proper.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:0f5ac9a6b3d15ba492a1199d7e9a1f0452e100eddcef87d2db90540ba00ccba2", "unit_id": "tag:01W0:prose-0004"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "01W0", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$f : X \\to Y$", "MATH_0003": "$S$", "MATH_0004": "$X$", "MATH_0005": "$S$", "MATH_0006": "$f$", "MATH_0007": "$Y$", "MATH_0008": "$S$", "MATH_0009": "$Y$", "MATH_0010": "$S$", "MATH_0011": "$Y$", "MATH_0012": "$S$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-image-proper-is-proper}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:cba3ab18cfaf35dbcb0290b47d8726bf0793313ecf4a4201d46187fbfeefb1d9", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:f47db6211b4db93f32fa2c696c1cd4850ff1d736d1ec5a391f60deb568d32592", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme. Let <MATH_0002> be a morphism of schemes over <MATH_0003>.\nIf <MATH_0004> is universally closed over <MATH_0005> and <MATH_0006> is surjective then\n<MATH_0007> is universally closed over <MATH_0008>. In particular, if also <MATH_0009> is\nseparated and locally of finite type over <MATH_0010>, then <MATH_0011> is proper over <MATH_0012>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:671ab4eb15f88ba35c0389226b7f29d653cad93ec7740feef55744bcc666b9fc", "unit_id": "tag:03GN:statement"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "01W0", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X$", "MATH_0002": "$f$", "MATH_0003": "$p : X \\to S$", "MATH_0004": "$q : Y \\to S$", "MATH_0005": "$S' \\to S$", "MATH_0006": "$f' : X_{S'} \\to Y_{S'}$", "MATH_0007": "$p' : X_{S'} \\to S'$", "MATH_0008": "$T \\subset Y_{S'}$", "MATH_0009": "$(f')^{-1}(T) \\subset X_{S'}$", "MATH_0010": "$p'((f')^{-1}(T)) = q'(T)$", "MATH_0011": "$q'$", "MATH_0012": "$Y \\to S$", "MATH_0013": "$Y \\to S$", "MATH_0014": "$Y \\to S$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-base-change-surjective}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-universally-closed-quasi-compact}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:e1ef50ed8c78732af6516332a29b0fd00b24dd8e6ed97408b77418a902f0d37c", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:f6a8598ad3f1fbc6dc7b8d8dd6feb17775a9a0eb47a87302ac2fa9f1a4d9dbf0", "source_text": "Assume <MATH_0001> is universally closed and <MATH_0002> surjective.\nDenote <MATH_0003>, <MATH_0004> the structure morphisms.\nLet <MATH_0005> be a morphism of schemes. The base change\n<MATH_0006> is surjective\n(Lemma <REF_0001>), and the base\nchange <MATH_0007> is closed.\nIf <MATH_0008> is closed, then <MATH_0009>\nis closed, hence <MATH_0010> is closed.\nSo <MATH_0011> is closed. This proves the first statement.\nThus <MATH_0012> is quasi-compact by\nLemma <REF_0002>\nand hence <MATH_0013> is proper by definition\nif in addition <MATH_0014> is locally of finite type and separated.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:1f2a05d7cb1a09ae6b1a3e986267896b81ebd81cb42403e4dd46f5bd97ebcd1c", "unit_id": "tag:03GN:proof"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "01W0", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\nX \\ar[rr]_h \\ar[rd]_f & & Y \\ar[ld]^g \\\\\n& S\n}\n$$", "MATH_0002": "$X \\to S$", "MATH_0003": "$Y \\to S$", "MATH_0004": "$Z \\subset Y$", "MATH_0005": "$h$", "MATH_0006": "$S$", "MATH_0007": "$X \\to Z$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-scheme-theoretic-image-is-proper}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:698076132bcb9a96d9c450a43a34a705636a80cd4167af991467890685e3da0d", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:f3c08de2822f9dd9e4708f5bb79f762788c91b4410667e26b1b390947e761c11", "source_text": "Suppose given a commutative diagram of schemes\n<MATH_0001>\nAssume\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> <MATH_0002> is a universally closed (for example proper) morphism, and\n<STRUCT_0003> <MATH_0003> is separated and locally of finite type.\n<STRUCT_0004>\nThen the scheme theoretic image <MATH_0004> of <MATH_0005>\nis proper over <MATH_0006> and <MATH_0007> is surjective.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:c13e61e4f209b1aca1f0685dd0fcceda413e1a9eeac7e594abdada7ec0c5d182", "unit_id": "tag:0AH6:statement"}
